{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481236-how-could-a-werewolf-ghost-become-ancestor-spirits","id":1481236,"title":"How could a werewolf ghost become Ancestor spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-16T07:48:10-07:00","id":1481236,"title":"How could a werewolf ghost become Ancestor spirits","content":"Hey, from what I have read around in the different editions one of the few sources of information regarding White howler available would be the ghost Cororuc who is currently hunting BSD or BSD ghosts in the dark umbra to kill them, and sometimes purify them. He currently have a small pack of what is considered White Howler ghost.<br /> <br /> In my setting the white howler have lost all of their ancestor spirits, they either fell to the BSD or were permanently destroyed when the tribe fell. I'm not super knowledgeable about wraith the Oblivion, most of what I read about ghost and such comes from werewolf (I purchased the book and plan to read it later).<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of a way to reinstate a ghost as an ancestor spirit but I'm falling short. What would you guys suggest for such a thing? It's not only regarding Cororuc, after all he found his purpose in the Shadowlands, but for the long run of the game. Would this simply no be possible, would there be any alternative ?<br /> <br /> Also should I involve the Silent striders? Since they have an ancestor, Tribal land and ghost issue there's a lot of point in common they would have with the players, except the fact that their land are far away from each other and the source of the problems very different. Right now there's not yet they have barely scratched the &quot;ghost topic&quot; so silent striders are mostly absent from the game. They are also not super present in Scotland were my player spend most of their time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8944,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","user":"Tanakyelle","date":".  Originally asking about ancestor spirit and ghost but I already asked it several year ago and got very interesting answers. Though don't hesitate if you have any idea 05-16-2022, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T08:21:55-07:00","id":1481239,"title":"","content":"I just realised that I already ask that to you years ago and have all the answer I could wish. <br /> <br /> If you guys don't mind I'll go for another topic. I've been working on Lion's brood (White Howler tribe totem). I'm using the W20 white Howler tribebook but I'm also adding some home made things. I was thinking of using the Barn owl as a spirit specialising in ghost knowledge. As an Owl it's not surprising that they could have this specialty and they used to be associated with ghosts and said to be the messenger of death in the middle age. My point of view is that even though Owl is the Tribe totem for the silent strider, it doesn't stop a specific owl-type to be attach to another brood. The same way rabbit and hare could be attached to different ones (I think that's actually the case but I'm not sure).<br /> <br /> The way I see the spirit is that, after the While Howler tribe fell, they saw omens saying that that the tribe would come back from the dead. Even though the BDS tried, the Owl Barn incarna was very powerful and even though many of her servant died, she didn't fell or disappeared. She rather distanced herself from werewolves, never being a pack totem again, waiting for her vision to Come true.<br /> She never spoke of this knowledge and never joined another brood, though she teaches brilliant Silent striders some of her wisdom and her gifts. She can also be persuaded to help bringing peace to a restless dead, but will always disappear when the problem is solved.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to differentiate her enough from Owl, or be more in a very specific range of knowledge/wisdom, I also want to make sure to keep her different from caern-rattler. I would see her spiritual correspondence being about The restless dead (Wraith, ghost and such) and the Dark Umbra. <br /> <br /> What could be her material correspondance and her taboos ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T10:10:00-07:00","id":1481245,"title":"","content":"It is not unusual in the canonical spirit broods for similar spirits to be found in different spirit broods.<br /> <br /> Some version of raven is found in the broods of Chimera (Dream Raven), Fenris (Hrafn), Thunder (Rogue Raven), Lion (Carrion Bird), and Griffin (WIld Raven is not listed in Axis Mundi, but does appear as a new totem in the Red Talons tribebook), as well as Raven itself (I assume that the Incarna of each Fera must also have their own brood). <br /> <br /> In the White Howler tribebook, it lists Roe Deer as part of Lion's brood even though in my opinion it would make better sense for that spirit to have always been in Stag's brood.<br /> <br /> You can find many other examples. You just call it something different and provide some flavor text to explain why this group of spirits have chosen a different Incarna to associate with.<br /> <br /> For example, rather than technically call it Barn Owl, you could use one its nicknames like &quot;Ghost Owl&quot;, &quot;Death Owl&quot;, or &quot;Lich Owl&quot; to distinguish this kind of owl spirit that is part of Lion's brood. You could have a story where some Barn Owl spirits went on a quest to the underworld, and required the protection of Lion for some reason. In exchange, they became part of Lion's brood and provide Lion with information on the underworld.<br /> <br /> For material correspondences, I'd keep it simple. You want something that makes sense for both it as a Barn Owl, and its spiritual correspondence. So on one hand, feathers of a barn owl, dead bodies of its prey animals, and so on plus things like human bones, cemeteries, and other associations with the dead for its wraithly aspects.<br /> <br /> As for taboos, maybe the spirit will never appear during the daytime or when the sun is out. It must either be night time or when the sky is so overcast the sun cannot be seen and light is dim. That makes sense for both a nocturnal animal and one associated with the dead. And since Barn Owls are known for not hooting, but hissing or screeching, maybe the spirit avoids certain kinds of noise or sounds. You could also do something like the spirit will never perform some kind of action - like it will only screech, requiring Spirit Speech, and never use or understand the Garou Tongue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T00:38:50-07:00","id":1481280,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much Black fox, this is amazing. I found your topic about spirit broods and plan to read it because it seems like quite a lot of informations and it could help me build Lion's brood.<br /> <br /> The players managed to approach Kelpie and there is a promise to join back Lion's brood depending on how they will end the scenario. I plan to use the each-uisge as well, I feel like they would be fitting well for the tribe : <br /> <br /> &quot;While the kelpie plies the rivers and streams of Scotland, the lochs and seas are home to the far more dangerous Each Uisge, literally the \u201cWater Horse\u201d. Each uisges are carnivorous, and relish human flesh. While other water-horses are content with playing pranks, tossing riders into ponds and laughing at their lot, an each uisge\u2019s actions are always predatory. In addition to hunting humans, they will also reproduce with farm animals, siring foals with flashing eyes, strong limbs, distended nostrils, and an indomitable spirit. Some people think the each-usige is a water spirit that guards the watery path to the afterlife where our ancestors live on. Its task is to test the person\u2019s worth. If it does not kill you then you are a judged worthy and carried to the underworld to join our forefathers&quot;<br /> <br /> And to find some contemporary spirits that may be willing to join lion's brood eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}